  <prompt>Add whole-invoice Reject (final, reason required) and Return to Firm (reason required; invoice becomes Returned to Firm, Inactive) for eligible approvers, each through 014 with exactly one Decision Record via 074, and link the accepted resubmission of a returned invoice to it through sprk_supersedesinvoice (D-43).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, idempotent decision writes and the Finance submission write path.</role>

  <goal>InvoiceRejectReturnEndpoints.cs and InvoiceRejectReturnService (reject, return), the supersedes link in 049's accept path, and tests proving authorization, reason rules, idempotency, rollup exclusion and the link.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-36 (acceptance: Returned / Rejected invoices excluded from rollups and the export; Duplicate rule ignores Rejected / Returned attempts for the same invoice number), FR-06 matrix (In Review → Rejected | Returned to Firm), FR-30 (exactly one Decision Record per reject / return), D-34, D-37 (resubmission keeps the firm invoice number, new .n via 045), D-43 (accepted resubmission = new invoice linked to the superseded one), I-4. Eligibility: 103's EligibleApproverResolver (any eligible approver may reject or return — prototype F-7 notes "Return to firm and Reject stay available to any eligible approver"). 012: sprk_supersedesinvoice lookup. 020: sprk_resubmissionof on the submission. Rollups count only FinanceBaseValues.CountedInvoiceStatuses (Services/Finance/FinanceBaseValues.cs; changed to statuscode In Review, Approved, Sent to AP, Paid by 015). Duplicate's exclusion of Rejected / Returned attempts is 071's handler. Export exclusion is enforced by 150. The firm notice and email are WP5 (131, 132): this task stores the reason and leaves the notification to 132.</background>
    <relevant-files>
