  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="074 ontology-r1 review K1/K3 (2026-10-17)">Recording billing Decision Records through BillingDecisionRecorder (074) brings two caller obligations.
- (1) Exactly-once. The writer is exactly-once only for retries made one after another; two concurrent calls with one decision id can both write, and a duplicate in an append-only ledger is permanent. So:
  - this task names its serialisation mechanism as an acceptance criterion. Examples: the job claims IIdempotencyService keyed by the decision id; an endpoint does a RowVersion-conditional status update and records only after it succeeds;
  - it adds a test for the concurrent same-id case.
- (2) Decider identity:
  - derive the deciding user from the authenticated principal, never from request input;
  - check invoice access through the UAC filter before recording;
  - pass no contact id. The recorder looks the contact up itself, as DecisionCommitService does; 074's fix round removes that parameter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-101 (2026-10-17)">A blocked or rejected submission already has its invoice (049 persists it). Return to firm sets that invoice to Returned to Firm through the lifecycle service, and its Decision Record files under the invoice (D-100 WriteBillingDecisionAsync). Do not add a submission lookup to sprk_decisionrecord.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-36">Reason required for both (400 ebilling.reason_required); reject and return only from In Review (409 otherwise); a second call after the invoice left In Review is a no-op with no new Decision Record.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-35 / F-7 default, root CLAUDE.md section 6">Only eligible approvers (103's live check) may reject or return: 403 ebilling.approver.not_eligible otherwise. Route filter "ebilling.invoice.decide".</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-30">Exactly one Decision Record per reject or return through 074's recorder; the approval portion status set to Rejected or Returned with decider and time.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-43">Only a Returned to Firm predecessor is linked: when a submission with the same firm and firm invoice number is accepted and the most recent prior invoice for that pair is Returned to Firm, the new invoice's sprk_supersedesinvoice points to it. A Rejected predecessor is never linked.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-001, ADR-008, ADR-019">Route conventions from 100; own endpoints file.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">Placement BFF (B1 caller identity, B4 live request); publish-size delta; no new HIGH CVE; no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="074 fix-round adversarial pass (2026-10-18), caller obligations of BillingDecisionRecorder">Callers that record billing decisions through BillingDecisionRecorder must:
- Derive the resolved Signal ids and the policy version id server-side, from the decision's own invoice and lines. Never take them from the request. The writer accepts any existing Signal or policy version (074 review K-2).
- Record before mutating, or run the recorder's reads first. Its refusals that depend on Dataverse reads (unknown policy version, missing Signal, undetermined subject, contact read fault) happen after Preflight, so a caller that changes invoice status first can be left with a changed status and no Decision Record (K-3).
- Serialise decisions per invoice (one at a time per invoice). The recorder's "already recorded" check and its create are not atomic (K-4).
- Build Values the same way on every attempt (same types, same decimal scale), so that an honest retry hashes to the same content (K-5, unless 074's follow-up normalises decimals).</constraint>
  </constraints>

