  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Read 103's service and notes, 074's actions, 049's accept path and 045's numbering; confirm 015 has changed CountedInvoiceStatuses.</step>
    <step order="1">Routes under /api/finance/invoices/{invoiceId} (names directional): POST reject, POST return (decision id, reason).</step>
    <step order="2">Service: eligibility, In Review check, 014 transition, portion update, 074 record — same exactly-once order as 103.</step>
    <step order="3">049 accept path: look up the most recent prior invoice for the firm and firm invoice number; link only if Returned to Firm.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests: reject and return happy paths; reason required; not eligible 403; not In Review 409; repeat is a no-op with one record; resubmission of a returned invoice is linked and of a rejected one is not; a Rejected or Returned invoice is excluded from the rollup query built from CountedInvoiceStatuses; contract tests 401 / 403 / disabled.</step>
    <step order="5">dotnet build and dotnet test green; publish-size delta and vulnerable-package check recorded.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="7">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Owner decided D-73 (F-7): Return of a blocked internal submission needs no privilege (105 implements it). Invoice Return here keeps its existing access rule; if that conflicts with D-73, STOP and align with 105.</trigger>
    <trigger>If 015 has not landed (rollups still read sprk_invoicestatus), STOP before the rollup test and report; do not add a statuscode filter here.</trigger>
    <trigger>If two prior invoices for the same firm and number are both Returned (ambiguous predecessor), STOP and confirm the rule (default: most recent by created on).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Spec section 11 row "Review / approval / export / rule endpoints"; 014 owns transitions, 074 the record, 103 eligibility; no reject / return route exists (InvoiceReviewService reject is "not an invoice" for documents, FinanceEndpoints.cs:51).</existing>
    <extension>Reuses 103's resolver and sequencing; own endpoints file; the supersedes link is one addition to the existing accept path rather than a new service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Reviewers cannot refuse or send back an invoice, resubmissions are unlinked from what they replace, and FR-36 and success criterion 5 fail.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">Api/Finance/InvoiceRejectReturnEndpoints.cs; Services/Finance/InvoiceRejectReturnService.cs; 049 accept path (supersedes link)</output>
    <output type="test">InvoiceRejectReturnServiceTests.cs; InvoiceRejectReturnEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Routes return 401 unauthenticated, 403 for a non-eligible caller, 503 ebilling.disabled when off, 409 when the invoice is not In Review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reject or return without a reason is 400 and writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reject moves the invoice to Rejected (Inactive), return to Returned to Firm (Inactive); each writes exactly one Decision Record and sets the portion status, decider and time; a repeated call writes no new record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An accepted resubmission for the same firm and invoice number of a Returned to Firm invoice is created with sprk_supersedesinvoice set to it; after a Rejected invoice it is not set.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Rejected and Returned invoices are excluded from the rollup set defined by CountedInvoiceStatuses (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build 0 errors; all tests green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>P4-C with 052 and 110: no file overlap (frontend). 049's accept path is shared with 103 / 105 edits that landed earlier in W4-2: re-read before editing. Export exclusion of Rejected / Returned invoices is 150's acceptance; Duplicate's exclusion is 071's (already tested there). Notification on Return / Reject is 132's; the firm-notice draft step in the decision wizard arrives with 131.</notes>

